<HelpTab>
    <HelpSection Title="Party Settings">
        <FluentText>
            <a href="/manage/parties/settings">Party Settings</a> is per location. Admins pick the <strong>Location</strong>;
            managers change the one they signed in to.
        </FluentText>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Timings</strong>: how long a party lasts, and how many minutes after arrival the children eat and play
                laser tag. These fill in the times when you book a party. Leave a time blank to leave that box empty. Press
                <strong>Save timings</strong> when you're done.</li>
            <li><strong>Hot food menu</strong>: the <strong>Meals</strong>, with their allergens, and the <strong>Sides</strong>
                offered with every meal.</li>
            <li><strong>Cold food menu</strong>: the <strong>Sandwiches</strong>, and the <strong>Other items in the box</strong>,
                which only appear in the allergy panel.</li>
        </ul>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpSection Title="Party staffing">
        <FluentText>
            Under <strong>Party staffing</strong> on Party Settings, say how many extra staff each type of party needs.
            <strong>Auto-build</strong> on the rota then adds those shifts for every booked party. It needs Staff Scheduling
            to be switched on.
        </FluentText>
        <ol>
            <li>Select <strong>Add party staffing</strong>.</li>
            <li>Under <strong>For</strong>, pick a party type you've used on bookings, <strong>Another type...</strong> to type
                one in, or <strong>Any other party</strong> for every type that has no staffing of its own.</li>
            <li>Choose the <strong>Position</strong> and <strong>How many</strong>, and how many minutes before the party
                they start and after it they finish.</li>
        </ol>
        <FluentText>
            Add one line per position, for example 2 Party Hosts and 1 Kitchen for "Lazer + Play". Types are matched to each
            booking's type ignoring capitals. The shift shows as "Party: " and the type, never the child's name.
        </FluentText>
        <FluentText>
            If a party is cancelled or its times change after Auto-build, the next Auto-build takes off the party's draft
            shifts and adds new ones. A shift you've already published is left alone, with a warning to change it yourself.
        </FluentText>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpSection Title="Printouts">
        <FluentText>
            <a href="/manage/parties/printouts">Printouts</a> lets you use your own artwork for the free return voucher and the
            feedback form. These apply at every location in your company. Without artwork, Lanyard prints its standard design with
            your logo and colour.
        </FluentText>
        <ol>
            <li>Export your blank design, with the boxes left empty, as a PNG or JPEG, and upload it.</li>
            <li>Set the <strong>Printed size</strong> in millimetres and choose <strong>Handwritten</strong> or <strong>Standard</strong> lettering.</li>
            <li>Under <strong>Boxes</strong>, choose <strong>What goes here</strong> for each box and position it in millimetres from
                the artwork's top-left corner. The drawing shows where every box goes; click a box on it to edit that one.
                <strong>Add a box</strong> and <strong>Reset to default positions</strong> are underneath.</li>
            <li>For the voucher, set how many months it's valid for after the party (12 by default, up to 60).</li>
            <li>Press <strong>Save</strong>, then <strong>Preview saved version</strong> to print a sample.</li>
        </ol>
        <FluentText>
            To go back to Lanyard's own design, press <strong>Remove artwork (use the standard design)</strong>, then <strong>Save</strong>.
        </FluentText>
    </HelpSection>
</HelpTab>
